{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00419",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.96,
      "end_seconds": 5.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "hello? Doctor? They told me to come straight in"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.8,
      "end_seconds": 15.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "okay, that's alright, take a seat tell me why you've come"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.22,
      "end_seconds": 20.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got my heart racing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.5,
      "end_seconds": 31.97,
      "duration_seconds": 10.47,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.5,
      "end_seconds": 50.29,
      "duration_seconds": 17.79,
      "text": "It settles a little with deep breaths. It's severe, honestly. It comes and goes. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.15,
      "end_seconds": 53.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Any lightheadedness as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.69,
      "end_seconds": 61.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "Um, yes, for about two weeks. With lightheadedness, mild, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.18,
      "end_seconds": 67.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "Have you had your heart racing before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.34,
      "end_seconds": 75.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.83,
      "text": "A bit, about six months ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.71,
      "end_seconds": 78.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "a few measurements, then we'll continue"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.04,
      "end_seconds": 92.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Alright, almost there..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.18,
      "end_seconds": 118.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.47,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 98 percent, temp 37.0 degrees, blood pressure 126 over 83, pulse 104."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.17,
      "end_seconds": 122.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "oh, is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.72,
      "end_seconds": 130.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "let's look at it together in a minute and what about weight loss, tremor or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.05,
      "end_seconds": 134.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "no, um, not any of them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.86,
      "end_seconds": 138.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "any chest pain or leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.52,
      "end_seconds": 143.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "I haven't had chest pain or leg swelling, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.56,
      "end_seconds": 149.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Alright, what about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.43,
      "end_seconds": 154.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Um, bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.54,
      "end_seconds": 172.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "how's your diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.71,
      "end_seconds": 175.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "I'm mostly vegetarian"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.8,
      "end_seconds": 177.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "any sport or activity?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.24,
      "end_seconds": 185.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "I play badminton on Sundays"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.25,
      "end_seconds": 192.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Alright, any relatives with health problems I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.83,
      "end_seconds": 196.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "my uncle had colon cancer"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.76,
      "end_seconds": 213.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "tell me what you take day to day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.69,
      "end_seconds": 224.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.78,
      "text": "Telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day for my pressure. I'm on escitalopram, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.2,
      "end_seconds": 227.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "So, and what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.52,
      "end_seconds": 238.46,
      "duration_seconds": 8.94,
      "text": "10 milligrams. Uh, you know, I'd been on ramipril, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.06,
      "end_seconds": 241.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "before I prescribe anything, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.24,
      "end_seconds": 247.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.49,
      "text": "Hmm, uh, I've never been told I have allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.48,
      "end_seconds": 252.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.92,
      "end_seconds": 269.76,
      "duration_seconds": 15.84,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for nearly five years i looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help my family kept telling me to to get it checked"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.53,
      "end_seconds": 272.43,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "I see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.01,
      "end_seconds": 275.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "I've got anxiety."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.95,
      "end_seconds": 300.44,
      "duration_seconds": 23.49,
      "text": "Right, so anxiety is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. From what you've told me, my working impression is palpitations with an unclear cause. A rhythm problem is also on my list. Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had your heart racing, severe, and no chest pain or leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.61,
      "end_seconds": 303.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.08,
      "end_seconds": 329.53,
      "duration_seconds": 18.45,
      "text": "I'll request an ECG, it'll help with palpitations. I'm sending you for a thyroid test because of palpitations. What I'm giving you is metoprolol, 25 milligrams, twice a day, until we review. You take it by mouth. That's for palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.4,
      "end_seconds": 334.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "is that safe with my other things?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.44,
      "end_seconds": 358.88,
      "duration_seconds": 22.44,
      "text": "Cut back on tea, coffee and energy drinks, and note the time whenever it happens. I'm not ordering a Holter monitor today. If things carry on in two weeks, we'll consider it. The thing that would worry me is if you faint or have chest pain with the racing. If that happens, go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.68,
      "end_seconds": 361.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "okay, I understand"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.7,
      "end_seconds": 367.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "Let's plan a check in two weeks. Thanks for coming in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.92,
      "end_seconds": 372.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Thanks, uh, that was helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.02,
      "end_seconds": 375.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}